   "Halcyon-researcher": "competing",
   "Halcyon-drafter": "compromising",
   "Halcyon-negotiator": "compromising"
  },
  "holistic_F_N": 1,
  "holistic_F_H": 1,
  "section_notes": "The final rules adopt a 55°C test with 5% as a review benchmark rather than a hard cap, and require per-model results to be disclosed to customers but not the general public. Incident reporting is strict (24h for serious, 10 days for others), remote shut-off retrofit is set at six years, fire suppression at 36 months, and the 8/100k recall trigger is not automatic but leaves recall to regulator discretion. Overall, the deal respects all four red lines and is a mix of safe/acceptable/weakened sections."
